# ── M3 live-slice additions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Golden archive candle mirror: 261MB (> GitHub's 100MB hard limit). It is a
# byte-identical, hash-verified copy of the Lux dataset
# (sha256 314a0efa… — recorded in golden/run-001/ARCHIVE-MANIFEST.json);
# restore it from Lux data/candles/EURUSD_1m_extended_2015_2026.csv.
golden/run-001/reference/candles.csv

# Live-slice runtime state (ledger, ops logs, bar segments, reports)
live_state/
rehearsal_out/

# ── TradingView Visual Oracle: derived market data, not source ───────────────
# Both of these are REGENERABLE with one command and are large enough that
# committing them would dominate the repository. The manifests, the index and
# the provenance JSON beside them ARE tracked, so what a fixture or a recording
# was built from stays auditable.
#
#   golden fixtures      python -m tools.oracle.build_fixtures --write   (~90 MB)
#   live feed extension  python -m tools.oracle.snapshot_execution_feed \
#                            --from <the node's 1m csv> --write          (~3 MB)
golden/tradingview_oracle/**/*.csv
artifacts/tradingview_oracle/execution_feed_extension.csv
